From 0f10023f8303495b941e347eab4bde3a7a1e781c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: axfor <aixiaoxiang2009@hotmail.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 02:18:34 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 36/36] lib/promscrape: send targets exposing increments a last
 acknowledgement on stop

A vmagent stopped while a scrape was on its way -- the target had written the
response and counted it delivered, the scrape was cancelled before it was
processed -- left the target holding that round, and the vmagent started after
it opens with AckNew, which commits it: the round was lost. Every graceful
restart and rolling deploy that came during a scrape lost one round per target.
With four such restarts end to end, v1.126.1031-cluster received 91.7M of
101.0M tokens written.

Once the scrapers have stopped, every target that had rounds and said it takes
one gets a last acknowledgement: the last round processed in full, on a request
of its own with X-Prometheus-Delta-Final. The target settles the round it holds
by it and takes nothing, so a round fetched and not processed is reported again
to the next vmagent instead. A scrape that was processing when the stop came
finishes first, so its round is the one acknowledged. It goes only to targets
whose rounds carry X-Prometheus-Delta-Features: final; others get nothing, as
before. Requests go out 64 at a time, each within 5 seconds.

Tests: the client sends it only to a target that said it takes one, with the
round and the header; on stop every target with rounds gets the last round
processed, one with none or without a client gets nothing; a scrape registers
its client. End to end with client_golang v1.24.1025, four restarts each during
a delivered response: 102,451,114 tokens written and received, every key exact.
